cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "fastesp: exact electrostatic potential from a Gaussian-basis wavefunction on the GPU"
abstract: >-
  Computes the electrostatic potential at arbitrary points from a MOLDEN
  wavefunction without real-space quadrature. The one-electron Coulomb integrals
  are evaluated in closed form via a Hermite (McMurchie-Davidson) expansion of
  the Gaussian product and Boys functions, contracted once per primitive pair
  into point-independent tables that a CUDA kernel then evaluates. On a 54-atom
  fragment (def2-TZVPPD, 1634 Cartesian functions) it is ~100x faster than
  Multiwfn at 300 surface points and >1000x at 30000 points, and agrees with an
  unscreened analytic evaluation to 1e-11 a.u.
authors:
  - family-names: Shu
    given-names: Zidong
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZidongS/fastesp"
type: software
